  "unit": "Unit 10 - Word Problems",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 10 - Word Problems for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br />\nA number increased by 7 is 20. Find the number.  </p>\n<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> = the number.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br />\nA rectangle has length 3 more than twice its width. If the perimeter is 42, find dimensions.  </p>\n<p>Let width = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>, length = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>42</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>42</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>6</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>36</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nRectangle: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>&#x000D7;</mi><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>Distance = rate × time.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br />\nA car travels 60 miles in the same time a train travels 100 miles. If the train is twice as fast, find car’s speed.  </p>\n<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = car speed. Train speed = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>.<br />\nTime = distance/rate.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Contradiction → no solution. Check: maybe train is <em>not exactly twice</em> but “20 mph faster.”  </p>\n<p><strong>Revised Problem</strong><br />\nCar: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, Train: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>, Times equal.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Cross-multiply: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nCar = 30 mph, Train = 50 mph.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>Work rate = 1 / (time to finish).  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br />\nAlice can paint a room in 4 hours, Bob in 6 hours. How long together?  </p>\n<p>Rates: Alice = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, Bob = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>. Together = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nSo time = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow></math> hours.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br />\nA 20-liter solution is 25% acid. How much water to add to make it 10% acid?  </p>\n<p>Acid = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> liters.<br />\nFinal solution: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> liters, still 5 acid.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Add 30 liters water.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<p><strong>Example 6</strong><br />\nFind three consecutive integers whose sum is 96.  </p>\n<p>Let numbers = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>96</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>96</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>93</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Numbers: 31, 32, 33.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Define variables before writing equations.  </li>\n<li>Watch out for <strong>“at least,” “at most”</strong> (inequalities).  </li>\n<li>Always answer in the <strong>context of the problem</strong> (no raw variables).  </li>\n<li>Plug answer choices back in if stuck (backsolving).  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) A number decreased by 8 is 15. What is the number?<br />\n2) A rectangle has width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>. If area = 75, find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>.<br />\n3) A plane flies 600 miles in the same time a car drives 200 miles. If plane speed is 4 times car speed, find speeds.<br />\n4) Two workers can finish a job in 5 hours together. If one works twice as fast as the other, how long alone for each?<br />\n5) A 40-liter mixture is 30% sugar. How much pure sugar to add to make it 50% sugar?  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) Car = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, Plane = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Contradiction → recheck wording. Likely: “Plane is 300 mph faster.”<br />\nTry: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Cross multiply: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>600</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>200</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>400</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow></math>. Car = 150 mph, Plane = 450 mph.  </p>\n<p>4) Let slow = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, fast = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Together rate = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Time = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>. So slow = 15 hrs, fast = 7.5 hrs.  </p>\n<p>5) Sugar initially = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>. Add <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> sugar → total sugar = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, total volume = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.<br />\nEquation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>.<br />\nAdd 16 liters sugar.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
